<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Cash offers steady to weak.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Cash offers steady to weak.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rail soymeal basis offers were steady to weak, with dealers attributing the pressure to ample supplies of soymeal and other feed ingredients.</p>
<p>Dealers said the weekly crush of 24.223 million, reported by the National Oilseed Processors Association early Friday, was too high for the demand. Exports and domestic feed use are weak creating an ample supply of soymeal.</p>
<p>Hot weather in the south and southeast has slowed hog and poultry feed consumption. Also, the advancing winter wheat harvest has made low-cost wheat available for feeding.  </p>
